    "content": "# GST Rates for Interior Design and Furniture Work in India\n\nInterior projects rarely sit under one tax rate. A single turnkey contract can touch 12%, 18%, and 28% across rows. This guide breaks down the current 2026 GST rates for the categories interior designers actually invoice.\n\n> This is general guidance, not legal advice. Always validate with your CA for project-specific situations.\n\n## Quick reference table\n\n| Category | HSN/SAC | GST Rate |\n|----------|---------|----------|\n| Interior design service (pure consultancy) | SAC 998391 | 18% |\n| Architectural service | SAC 998322 | 18% |\n| Works contract (residential interior, supply + fix) | SAC 9954 | 18% |\n| Wooden furniture, modular kitchen carcass | HSN 9403 | 18% |\n| Plywood, particle board, MDF | HSN 4410 / 4411 | 18% |\n| Laminate sheets | HSN 4823 | 18% |\n| Veneer | HSN 4408 | 18% |\n| Paint, varnish | HSN 3208 / 3209 | 18% |\n| Tiles (ceramic) | HSN 6907 | 18% |\n| Marble, granite (slabs) | HSN 2515 / 2516 | 18% |\n| Sanitary ware, faucets | HSN 7324 / 8481 | 18% |\n| LED lights, fixtures | HSN 9405 | 12% |\n| Switches, wires | HSN 8536 / 8544 | 18% |\n| Curtains, upholstery fabric | HSN 6303 / 5407 | 12% |\n| Carpets | HSN 5703 | 12% |\n| Glass (toughened) | HSN 7005 / 7007 | 18% |\n| Air conditioners | HSN 8415 | 28% |\n\n## How to assign the right rate\n\nThree rules:\n\n1. **Pure service = SAC + 18%.** Design fee, supervision, consultation.\n2. **Pure goods = HSN of the item.** Most furniture and materials = 18%.\n3. **Composite supply (supply + installation) = works contract = 18%** under SAC 9954.\n\nFor example, a modular kitchen installation invoice with cabinets, hardware, granite top, sink, and chimney is a *composite supply* — even though the chimney alone might attract 28% as a standalone good. The dominant nature is works contract, so the entire composite attracts 18%.\n\n## What about that 28% on air conditioners?\n\nIf you supply and install a split AC as part of a turnkey contract, it can be argued as composite supply at 18%. If you sell the AC as a standalone good with no installation bundled, it remains 28%. Your accountant will pick the position based on your invoicing pattern.\n\nWhen in doubt, split into two invoices: a goods invoice at the item rate, a service invoice at 18% for installation.\n\n## Worked example — a 3BHK turnkey\n\n| Item | Value | Rate | Tax |\n|------|-------|------|-----|\n| Modular kitchen (composite) | 4,80,000 | 18% | 86,400 |\n| Wardrobes (composite) | 5,60,000 | 18% | 1,00,800 |\n| False ceiling | 1,20,000 | 18% | 21,600 |\n| Painting | 90,000 | 18% | 16,200 |\n| Electrical (works contract) | 1,40,000 | 18% | 25,200 |\n| LED light fixtures (standalone supply) | 60,000 | 12% | 7,200 |\n| Curtains (supply only) | 80,000 | 12% | 9,600 |\n| Design fee | 1,50,000 | 18% | 27,000 |\n| **Total** | **16,80,000** | — | **2,94,000** |\n\nNotice that LED fixtures and curtains stay at 12% because they were billed as standalone goods, not as part of a works contract.\n\n## Common rate disputes\n\n- **\"Modular kitchen is furniture, so 28%.\"** No — modular kitchen with installation is composite works contract at 18%.\n- **\"Marble is 28%.\"** No — marble slabs are 18%.\n- **\"My CA said 12% for the design fee.\"** Pure design service is 18% (SAC 998391). 12% applies to certain notified services, not interior design consultancy in general.\n\n## Practical advice\n\nMaintain an HSN/SAC + rate column in your item library. Every quotation auto-fills the correct rate per row. This is the single biggest defence against rate errors.\n\nIntorza ships with a pre-loaded interior-specific HSN/SAC library so your first invoice is compliant on day one.\n\n## What to do next\n\nAudit your last 5 invoices. Are HSN/SAC codes present per row? Are works-contract rates applied correctly? Two hours of cleanup today saves a notice tomorrow.\n\nRead the broader playbook: [GST invoice for interior designers in India](/blog/gst-invoice-interior-designers-india-guide).\n"
